1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
Why Domain Matters, part 2: Logistics and supply chain. The record says delivered on time, in full; one pallet line held the wrong pack size.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:10,800
The same synthetic world: Store 014 in Jayanagar, the warehouse in Hoskote, and an answer key that knows every pallet.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:17,700
Five readings: the dashboard says 88%, the data tests pass, the corrections net to ₹80, and the assistant says in full.

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:25,100
Every record of line 1 says 5 kg. The pallet held 160 packs of 1 kg. All were written from one scan of the slot.

5
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:31,500
The books said 63. The shelf was empty for 51.5 open hours, and nothing was reordered.

6
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:38,400
10 data tests pass. Five tests about how a warehouse works fail; none of June's 30 pallets was checked by anything but the pick.

7
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:45,800
Pair the corrections: equal and opposite in cases, in each building and across the two. Gross ₹44,648, net ₹80.

8
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:52,200
The demo: change what the data team does with June's records, or rerun June with the warehouse and the store checking pallets.

9
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:59,600
The trace: one 16-case pick of 5 kg in the week before, SHP-260622 line 1. The answer key: 160 packs of 1 kg.

10
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:07,000
With a domain layer the assistant answers 7 of 7: not theft, not in full, and the claim belongs to line 1 of the 22 June truck.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,900
OTIF four ways: 92%, 90%, 88%, 84%. Reconciled with counts, the records give 84% too.

12
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:20,300
Scan every case at pick: the mistake never happens. OTIF stays 88%, and now it is true.

13
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:26,700
Weigh every pallet: caught at dispatch, the truck arrives late. OTIF falls to 84%; the shelf stays full.

14
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:33,100
Scan every case at the store: caught on arrival. OTIF falls to 84% again, because it now counts what arrived.

15
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:39,500
The technical companion: the tests in SQL, the mirror pairs, the trace, OTIF reconciled, and a notebook on the records.

16
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:45,900
For data and AI leaders: five questions to ask your team.

17
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:51,400
Every record agreed. That is exactly why nobody checked the pallet.
